-- title:
--   Ogg's unit Δ(q)/Δ(qᵖ): integrality and level Γ_H(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ and $M$ be natural numbers with $p$ prime and $M$ nonzero, let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and assume $p \mid M$. Write $u =$ `modularUnitSeries p` for the Laurent series $\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^p) \in \mathbb{Q}((q))$, that is the product of $\Delta(q) = q\prod_{n\ge 1}(1-q^n)^{24}$ (the rational Laurent series $q$ times the power series `dedekindEtaUnitQ`) with the inverse of its image under the substitution $q \mapsto q^p$. The assertion is a fourfold conjunction: first, there is a Laurent series $x$ over $\mathbb{Z}$ whose coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Q}$ equals $u$, whose coefficient in degree $1-p$ equals $1$, and whose coefficients in all degrees $n < 1-p$ vanish; second, $u$ lies in the intermediate field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CohCarrier.GammaH M H)` of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$, namely the subfield generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by all quotients of $q$-expansions of modular forms of some weight for $\Gamma_H(M)$ admitting integral $q$-expansions (with nonzero denominator), where $\Gamma_H(M) \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ is the preimage in $\Gamma_0(M)$ of $H$ under the lower-right-entry character $\Gamma_0(M) \to (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$; third, $u$ is integral over the $\mathbb{Q}$-subalgebra of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the $q$-expansion `jq` $= q^{-1}(1 + \cdots)$ of the modular invariant $j$; and fourth, $u^{-1}$ is integral over that same subalgebra.
--
--   This packages the basic properties of Ogg's modular unit $\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^p)$ on $X_0(p)$: it has a primitive integral $q$-expansion beginning with $q^{1-p}$, it is a function of level $\Gamma_H(M)$ whenever $p \mid M$, and together with its inverse it is integral over $\mathbb{Q}[j(q)]$, so that its divisor is supported on the cusps. It is used downstream in the analysis of cuspidal places and of the reductions of level structures, for instance in the criteria distinguishing cuspidal from non-cuspidal specialisations.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_int_coeffMap_eq_modularUnitSeries_and_mem_qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH_of_dvd.lean

